  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThis strategy target improves the Erd\u0151s discrepancy bound by:\n- Using Gaussian mixture models parametrization to represent the solution\n- Employing a boosted search strategy with multiple probability distributions\n- Maintaining a record of Pareto-optimal solutions across different resolutions\n- Using strong correlation with history of best-known solutions\n- Fallback to binary/local search for unsolved instances\n\nThe approach addresses the optimization's non-convexity by:\n- Using RBF interpolation to smooth the objective landscape\n- Application of filterSQP for constrained optimization\n- Dynamic weighting of different lags in the correlation metric\n- Self-adaptive mutation in the search process\n\nBottlenecks addressed: \n- Previous method over-emphasized short-term refinement\n- New approach maintains diversity through multiple nested scales\n- Overcoming local optima via adaptive restarts\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n- Representation: h(x) = \u03a3 w_i \u03d5_i(x) where \u03d5_i are RBF kernels\n- Objective: minimize max_k [ \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)\u00b7(1-h(x+k)) dx ]\n- Constraint: \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1, 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1\n- Probability distributions: \n  - Ring-shaped Gaussian (mean shift 1.5, \u03c3=1)\n  - Smoothened uniform mixture (max variance sweep)\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\ndef run(seed=42, budget_s=1100, **kwargs):\n    start_time = time.time()\n    total_time = budget_s - 20\n    \n    if 'initial_h_values' in kwargs:\n        old_parent = kwargs['initial_h_values']\n        old_n = len(old_parent)\n    else:\n        old_parent, old_n = None, None\n    \n    n_points = determine_starting_resolution(time.time(), old_n, budget_s)\n    h = initialize_h(n_points, seed)\n    \n    # Main optimization with filterSQP\n    try:\n        # Adapting the objective function for RBF representation\n        def obj(x):  \n            # Compute correlation and objective score\n            dx = 2.0 / n_points\n            c = np.correlate(x, 1-x, mode='full')\n            return float(np.max(c) * dx)\n        \n        # Constraints handling via penalty\n        def cons(x):\n            sum_d = np.sum(x)\n            dx = 2.0 / n_points\n            return [sum_d - sum_d + n_points/4], [ -x.min(), x.max()-1]  # illustrative\n            \n        res = minimize(obj, h, method='SLSQP', bounds=[(0,1)]*n_points,\n                        constraints=cons, options={'maxiter':3000})\n        \n        if res.success:\n            h = res.x\n            candidate_score = float(np.max(np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full') * dx)\n    \n    except:\n        # Implement recovery procedure\n        pass\n    \n    # Maintain resolution history\n    return h, candidate_score, n_points\n\n4. Search choices:\n- Resolution sweep: n_points \u2208 {200, 300, 400, 600, 800}\n- Objective weighting: lag weighting with 1/k^2 for covariance scores\n- Convexification: use sigmoid weighting [0,1] -> (-\u221e, \u221e)\n- Mutation strength history: adaptive change with discovery probability\n\n5. Compute budget:\n- Phase1: 150s (local search)\n- Phase2: 400s (convexification)\n- Phase3: 300s (resolution increase)\n- Final polishing: 250s\n\n6. Validation and fallback:\n- Integral check: enforce sum(h)*dx=1\u00b11e-4\n- Auto-correlation diagnostics: detect flat peaks\n- If n_points=400 fails: fall back to binary GA with n=600\n- If time below 500s: return seed-based preliminary solution",
